# The relay's origin — a BARE origin, no path.
#
# Vite inlines import.meta.env at build time and never reads it at runtime, so this is a
# build-time value: in CI it belongs wherever that build's environment variables are set
# (a Workers Builds variable, if that is how this deploys), not in the deployed Worker.
#
# Everything in the table appends its own path to it — /room/new, /token, /parties/room/<code>
# — so pasting an endpoint URL rather than an origin silently produces requests that match no
# route on the relay, with a dead multiplayer tab and nothing in the console as the only
# symptom. multiplayer.js normalises the value defensively for exactly that reason, but it is
# cheaper to write it correctly.
#
# Unset falls back to ws://localhost:8787, which is what `npm --workspace cardcarp-relay run dev`
# serves — so local development needs no .env at all.
VITE_MULTIPLAYER_WS_URL=https://cardcarp-relay.ben-r-b39.workers.dev
